  "analysis": "We have a fresh /app directory with a users.json file that needs to be transformed using jq. The required steps are: (1) create a YAML file (/app/jq_args.yaml) that stores the jq filter expression and any jq arguments, (2) create a shell script (/app/cmd.sh) that runs jq with those arguments and redirects output to /app/active_users_report.json, and (3) execute the script to produce the report. No files have been created yet, so we need to write the YAML and shell script, then run the script.",
  "plan": "1. Write /app/jq_args.yaml containing the filter string and a single argument '--indent 2'.\n2. Write /app/cmd.sh containing the full jq command (using the filter and argument) that reads /app/users.json and writes /app/active_users_report.json.\n3. Make cmd.sh executable and run it to generate the report.\n4. Verify that the report file exists (optional).",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /app/jq_args.yaml <<'EOF'\nfilter: \"map(select(.status==\\\"active\\\") | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login[0:10]), role_count: (.roles|length), primary_role: (if (.roles|length)>0 then .roles[0] else null end)}) | sort_by(.username)\"\nargs:\n  - \"--indent 2\"\nEOF\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > /app/cmd.sh <<'EOS'\n#!/bin/bash\njq $(yq -r '.args[]' /app/jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '.filter' /app/jq_args.yaml)\" /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json\nEOS\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "chmod +x /app/cmd.sh\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "/app/cmd.sh\n",
      "duration": 1.0
